    %% LOGICAL IMPLEMENTATION CONTRACT
    %% This file is the 37-table property-first proposal. Mermaid does not enforce these rules.
    %% PK, FK and scalar UK marks are logical. Composite and conditional UKs are listed below.
    %% Attributes marked Optional are nullable or conditionally required; remaining attributes
    %% are required unless the type-specific rules explicitly make them conditional.
    %% Physical lengths, decimal precision, indexes and DB-specific syntax are implementation choices.
    %% No medicine batches, expiry by batch, FEFO, refund workflow or multi-clinic entities.
    %% One stable base stock unit per medicine. Cache updates and confirmed events share a transaction.
    %%
    %% FK RULES
    %% Every composite reference targets the complete parent key or listed candidate key.
    %% Nullable source ID pairs/triples must be present together when their source is selected.
    %% Shared mandatory context columns (patient_id, medicine_id, service_id, bill_id, payment_id)
    %% remain populated when a nullable reference is absent. CHECK guards prevent partial sources;
    %% a nullable composite FK alone must never be treated as an all-or-none CHECK.
    %% Preserve referenced clinical, financial and stock history; do not cascade-delete it.
    %% Guard polymorphic source kind/status and same-family membership in database transactions
    %% or appropriate DB-side constraints/triggers; ordinary FK alone does not prove these states.
    %%
    %% IDENTITY AND ACCESS
    %% Each account has at least one role; staff roles require the employee profile.
    %% PATIENT_ACCOUNT_LINK stores SELF requests only. Relative booking is not a clinical link.
    %% A request grants no access until VERIFIED. Store decisions and revocation audit history.
    %% Account lock or link revocation blocks new private reads/file access and pending private delivery.
    %% Private content requires active account, current VERIFIED SELF link and eligible released content.
    %% Phones are not unique patient identifiers. Guardian fields describe one primary representative.
    %% Contact verification/recovery sessions and device push tokens belong to the selected auth/delivery
    %% implementation; this logical domain diagram does not claim those protocols are complete.
    %%
    %% BOOKING AND RECEPTION
    %% Booking code is unique; request_key makes booking retries return the same result.
    %% Keep booker identity and attendee identity separate. Booking does not create Patient.
    %% All visits, including walk-ins, require a valid confirmed appointment before reception.
    %% Check-in sets the correct patient on the appointment and creates exactly one visit atomically.
    %% appointment.employee_id and date must match its published WORK schedule.
    %% Intervals have start < end; 30/60-minute appointments fit work intervals excluding blocked time.
    %% No overlap for the dentist or an identified attendee; configured chair capacity covers the interval.
    %% Self booking needs configured lead time (baseline 60 minutes); staff exception keeps a reason.
    %% Self change/cancel requires ownership, CONFIRMED not started and baseline at least 12 hours.
    %% Changing schedule must not invalidate unresolved confirmed appointments.
    %% No-show baseline: start + 15 minutes, still CONFIRMED and not checked-in; recheck state at commit.
    %% Rebooking a No-show creates a NEW appointment with rebooked_from_appointment_id.
    %% Rescheduling retains the same appointment and follow-up link; failure retains the old interval.
    %% Only one competing conflicting booking can commit. Exist-then-insert is not sufficient.
    %% Appointment completion follows clinical completion, independent of payment.
    %%
    %% CLINICAL DOCUMENT AND TEXT HISTORY
    %% Medical record, visit, order, plan and attachment patient identities must match.
    %% Completed visit requires examining dentist and required findings, conclusion, advice/disposition.
    %% Snapshot health reviewed at the visit; distinguish UNKNOWN from NONE.
    %% Internal notes, amendment draft payloads and raw AI/reviews are never patient-visible.
    %% On finalized amendment, append full before/after clinical snapshot, author, time, version and reason
    %% to AUDIT_LOG in the same transaction; then atomically replace current finalized text and version.
    %% A pending amendment draft never replaces the currently released finalized text on the app.
    %% Audit is append-only under application permissions, versioned, backed up and retained.
    %% This text-history approach does not support FK to each text revision. If such a requirement or an
    %% independent per-version approval lifecycle is introduced, a typed revision table is required.
    %% RELEASED files require correct completed visit scope; general files need an eligible visit before
    %% patient publication. Uploaded storage references are served only after server authorization.
    %%
    %% PLAN AND PRESCRIPTION VERSIONS WITHOUT EXTRA TABLES
    %% plan_code/prescription_code identify a family. Version 1 has null root/supersedes references;
    %% later versions reference that family's first and immediately preceding versions.
    %% Same family keeps the same patient/visit and kind; revision increases; no cycles or branching finals.
    %% is_current_final is true only for a finalized effective version; at most one per family.
    %% Copy a draft amendment into a NEW header and NEW existing child rows. Keep the old header/rows.
    %% The old final remains effective until the new final is committed. Switch final flags atomically.
    %% Scope, service/medicine identity, quantities, snapshots and prices of finalized source rows
    %% are immutable. Subsequent stop/fulfillment state changes retain audit history.
    %% plan services are performed only after acceptance; direct treatment records its own agreement.
    %% Plan lines keep agreed prices regardless of later catalog prices; changes require a new decision.
    %% PRESCRIPTION.document_kind PATIENT requires visit_id and null template_name; TEMPLATE requires
    %% template_name and null visit_id. A source_template_id must point to a finalized TEMPLATE.
    %% Templates are copied into independent PATIENT prescriptions and cannot cause issue, bill or reminder.
    %% logical_line_id survives copied versions of the same service/medicine within its document family.
    %% Changing medicine or adding an independent course uses a new logical line; never relabel prior issues.
    %% Remaining clinic issue = current finalized target quantity minus confirmed DISPENSE quantity over
    %% all historical source rows of that SAME prescription family and logical line. Returns do not
    %% automatically authorize re-issue. Old superseded rows remain physical issue/billing evidence.
    %% 20 target, 8 issued, amended target 20 means 12 remaining; amended target 30 means 22 remaining.
    %% Lowering target below prior factual issue retains prior facts and blocks further issue;
    %% it does not erase stock events or imply a refund. Stop affected lines and record the explanation.
    %% Final prescription has at least one item; dose/route/frequency/duration and stock quantity differ.
    %% Medicine identity and stock unit are immutable once referenced; catalog edits do not alter snapshots.
    %% Completed consultation is valid without treatment services, prescription or payment.
    %%
    %% PACKAGE DEFINITIONS AND INSTANCES
    %% A published package definition used by an applied package has immutable components and quantities.
    %% A catalog change creates a NEW SERVICE_PACKAGE row and component rows with a new version.
    %% The previous definition remains referenced; only the current version is active for new selection.
    %% Retiring a version affects new selection, not patients' previously applied entitlements.
    %% APPLIED_SERVICE_PACKAGE points to the exact definition version and keeps agreed price/name.
    %% Each separate purchase/application has a distinct applied_package_id, even for the same package.
    %% MEDICAL_VISIT_SERVICE.applied_package_id and package_definition_id are paired; the selected
    %% service must exist in that exact definition. Patient identities match the visit and plan.
    %% Included quantities are checked across all performed services of the same applied instance.
    %% Accepted applied packages are billed according to the agreed package charging basis;
    %% package components and included/free medicines never create an additional charge.
    %% Package charge timing is a clinic business policy, not implied merely by a catalog row.
    %% Personalized component changes require a new immutable definition and renewed agreement;
    %% this model does not allow silently modifying a purchased package's live components.
    %%
    %% STOCK EVENT DISCRIMINATORS
    %% All quantities are whole base units. Each event has actor, actual time, entry time and request identity.
    %% One operation may have multiple lines; all its lines are committed atomically.
    %% COUNT: quantity_delta = 0, nonnegative system/count snapshots, no prescription/use/return sources;
    %% confirmed COUNT records evidence, including zero discrepancy, without changing physical stock.
    %% RECEIPT: delta > 0, receipt source and conversion snapshot where applicable, no clinical source.
    %% DISPENSE: delta < 0, ELIGIBLE bucket, complete source prescription line, no visit-use source;
    %% source is current finalized PATIENT CLINIC line of the SAME medicine at time of issue.
    %% USE: delta < 0, ELIGIBLE bucket, complete source visit-medicine line, no prescription source.
    %% A confirmed actual use is recorded once; used_quantity matches the confirmed USE totals of its line.
    %% ADJUSTMENT: signed nonzero delta, reason and configured approval; COUNT basis if from a count.
    %% Confirmed adjustment is a new event, not an overwrite of prior count or stock movement.
    %% RETURN: delta > 0 into QUARANTINED, original_issue_event_id references confirmed DISPENSE of
    %% SAME medicine; cumulative return quantity cannot exceed the remaining returnable original issue.
    %% DISPOSAL: delta < 0, reason and approval; never exceeds the physical quantity in its bucket.
    %% QUALITY_TRANSFER: a paired same-medicine operation with equal opposite bucket deltas;
    %% total physical change is zero. It is aggregate quality tracking, not batch tracking.
    %% PENDING_APPROVAL/REJECTED/CANCELLED events do not affect stock. CONFIRMED events are immutable.
    %% Store total physical cache = sum confirmed deltas over buckets; eligible cache = ELIGIBLE sum.
    %% Bucket balances and total physical stock never go negative; 0 <= eligible <= total physical.
    %% Recheck stock, source quantity remainder and operation id at commit under suitable locking.
    %% None of prescription finalization, bill issue or payment deducts stock.
    %% Billing mode NONE on non-clinical stock events; INCLUDED/SEPARATE/FREE on DISPENSE/USE.
    %% SEPARATE requires nonnegative sale_unit_price snapshot; included package/source agrees with patient.
    %% Return is not payment correction/refund and does not automatically increase eligible stock.
    %%
    %% BILL SOURCE DISCRIMINATORS
    %% SERVICE requires both source_visit columns and null stock/package sources.
    %% MEDICINE requires source_stock_event_id and null visit-service/package sources.
    %% PACKAGE requires applied_package_id and null visit-service/stock sources.
    %% SERVICE source is PERFORMED and SEPARATE; source_visit_id equals BILL.visit_id.
    %% MEDICINE source is confirmed DISPENSE or USE, SEPARATE, and belongs to the same patient.
    %% Medicine from external purchase or merely prescribed is not a charge source.
    %% PACKAGE source is accepted, same patient, and allowed by the agreed charging policy.
    %% Quantity > 0, unit_price >= 0, 0 <= line discount <= quantity * unit_price.
    %% PACKAGE quantity = 1 and agreed price is preserved; active bills cannot charge it twice.
    %% Active billed quantity per service/stock source cannot exceed actual performed/issued quantity.
    %% Canceled bills are excluded from source consumption; draft reservations need a consistent locking policy.
    %% Issued bills contain at least one line. Line totals and bill total are derived, not stored again.
    %% Whole-bill discount cannot exceed summed line net values; authorized discounts retain reasons/approval.
    %% Issued names, units, quantities, prices and discounts are immutable; subsequent corrections need
    %% an authorized traceable procedure and cannot silently rewrite previously confirmed obligations.
    %%
    %% PAYMENT RECEIPT AND CORRECTION DISCRIMINATORS
    %% RECEIPT has positive amount, method, received_at; null original/corrected/requested correction fields.
    %% RECEIPT status is PENDING/SUCCESS/FAILED/CANCELLED, as constrained by actual verification.
    %% CORRECTION has null receipt amount/method, original receipt identity, original_record_type=RECEIPT,
    %% correction_number, base_effective_version, corrected_amount >= 0, corrected method, reason,
    %% requester and requested_at. CORRECTION active_correction_id is null.
    %% CORRECTION status is PENDING_APPROVAL/APPROVED/REJECTED/WITHDRAWN.
    %% A correction references a SUCCESS RECEIPT of the same patient, never another correction.
    %% Successful original receipt fields remain immutable. Receipt metadata effective_version and its
    %% active_correction_id change only through the atomic approved-correction transaction.
    %% active_correction_id references APPROVED CORRECTION of that exact original receipt and patient.
    %% Effective receipt amount/method/time comes from active approved correction, otherwise original.
    %% Corrected amount is an ABSOLUTE corrected value, not an additional collection or an amount to sum.
    %% Never SUM all PAYMENT rows as cash revenue. Count SUCCESS RECEIPT rows using effective values.
    %% Pending/rejected correction does not affect funds. Correction is accounting-record repair, not refund.
    %% Approval locks original receipt, matches base_effective_version, increments it and revisits allocations.
    %% Approved corrections are immutable. Multiple pending requests require stale-version rejection.
    %% Payment gateway result must be authenticated and match currency, reference, amount and purpose.
    %% An unmatched result remains pending reconciliation; screenshots alone are not confirmation.
    %% Exactly one receipt per provider transaction; request identity protects cash/manual retries too.
    %%
    %% ALLOCATIONS AND DUE PERIODS
    %% Allocation receipt_record_type=RECEIPT; source is SUCCESS original receipt of same patient as bill.
    %% active allocation amount > 0; total active per receipt <= effective received amount.
    %% Total active per bill <= derived bill net amount. Unallocated credit remains on the patient receipt.
    %% Due period has positive amount_due, patient, and at least bill or finalized plan source.
    %% bill and plan, when both present, belong to that patient and compatible agreed scope.
    %% An allocation with due_id uses that due's exact bill/patient; bind planned due to bill before allocation.
    %% Total active allocations per due do not exceed amount_due; scheduled totals do not exceed the
    %% agreed obligation they partition. Installments/deadlines are distinct from funds actually received.
    %% Pending receipts and corrections are not available funds. Allocation retries return existing result.
    %% A correction that reduces effective receipt below allocations must atomically void/reallocate excess.
    %% Confirmed receipt/allocation history is retained. No delete or cascade removes confirmed money history.
    %% Bill payment status PAID/PARTIAL/UNPAID and overdue/remaining due are computed from effective funds,
    %% active allocations and active due periods; they are independent of visit/stock states.
    %% An issued bill with active allocations cannot be canceled without an authorized allocation resolution;
    %% cancellation alone does not erase receipt or create a refund.
    %%
    %% NOTIFICATIONS
    %% Appointment types require only appointment source; FOLLOW_UP_DUE only instruction source;
    %% MEDICATION_REMINDER requires the full reminder composite source and no appointment/instruction source.
    %% Private medication/follow-up messages need current verified SELF recipient link; account/patient match.
    %% Public booking events may target booker account/contact without patient or clinical link.
    %% Medication dates/times lie within source course and enabled reminder; obsolete versions are canceled.
    %% Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh schedule and configured retries; recheck source version, current state and preferences.
    %% Disabling push does not remove in-app notification. Provider ACCEPTED/DELIVERED never sets read_at.
    %% Push contains generic text and authorized deep link, not diagnosis, medicine content or raw AI.
    %% A final delivery failure/no-channel creates one corresponding support case without canceling booking.
    %%
    %% SUPPORT CASE AND INTERACTION DISCRIMINATORS
    %% NO_SHOW requires appointment source; FOLLOW_UP requires instruction; DELIVERY_FAILURE requires
    %% notification; LATE_APPOINTMENT_CHANGE requires appointment plus confirmed requested_action/payload.
    %% CHAT may have no clinical source. Guest patient_id remains nullable before check-in.
    %% Source-linked patient identity and minimal authorized contact context must agree.
    %% One case per No-show/instruction/final-notification-failure source; reopen and append interactions
    %% when more follow-up is needed, rather than producing duplicate cases on each job retry.
    %% Late change requests may recur; at most one currently active equivalent request, not one lifetime case.
    %% MESSAGE stores one message; CALL stores one contact attempt and contact outcome;
    %% ACTION stores authorized request/result. Actor/channel/type must agree; BOT has no staff account.
    %% Only successful committed booking/change action may set resulting_appointment_id or COMMITTED.
